Hi Finn,

I extended my model to a hurdle model. First, I defined SPDE as you said:
  spde <- inla.spde2.matern(mesh, constr=TRUE)

The model formula is
form <-  y ~  -1 + f(year.z, model="iid")  + f(year.y, model="iid") + f(sy, model=spde, replicate=sy.repl) + f(sz, copy='sy', replicate=sz.repl,fixed=FALSE)

In the model, z is catch occurrence variable, and y is catch rate variable.

I got results on year effects:
 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-yCzWdH1luYY/WOq8A80E8vI/AAAAAAAAAc8/mtY0nDps9asXDm0_T9ARBjWR0qazDtljQCLcB/s1600/2.year.jpeg>

I am wondering why the year effect on z is still flat??

Thanks,
Ruby

